  "scope": "One fresh disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster with one control-plane node and two labeled workers. A single non-privileged synthetic HTTP Pod is pinned to worker-a and exposed by one NodePort Service. The same Service, endpoint, port, and localhost-to-worker mappings are probed with explicit externalTrafficPolicy Cluster and Local values. Harmless GET requests compare the endpoint-free worker with the endpoint worker. This is a kube-proxy/Kind behavior fixture, not production approval or documentation evidence. It does not establish a cloud LoadBalancer, healthCheckNodePort behavior, client source IP preservation across Docker/Kind address rewriting, provider defaults, or production endpoint topology and availability. No public destination or packet injection is used.",
